      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Some suggestion how security concerns could be handled:\n\n- Interacting with a GameObject that triggers a link should open a popup which the world creators can't prevent. This popup should show the URL and ask the user if they are sure to open the link.\n\n- Additionally, users should be able to report links (via a button within that popup) similar to reddit, Twitter, etc. These links then would be verified by the moderation team.\n\n- VRC could implement a safety setting which defaults to \"Block all links\". Users then must manually disable it in order to click on links. This is similar to the custom video URL safety setting.\n\nI explicilty don't want an ingame browser since that is hard to implement and could lead to security issues if implemented wrongly.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-10-03T11:18:53.793Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "A nice ability for world creators would be if you can interact with something which then opens a link in your browser.\n\nExample: Many world creators have Discord or Patreon links in their world on a wall. A user then have to get out of VR to type that link manually into their browser or taking a screenshot to do later so. \n\nIt would be much easier if you just could interact with that link directly (VRC_Trigger -> OnInteract)",
